harness: scripts/ladder_vs_cjxl.py
command: scripts/ladder_vs_cjxl.py --ours target/release/cjxl-rs \
           --cjxl .ci-libjxl/tools/cjxl --out <tsv> --reps 5 <png>...
         (--reps 3 for the 2048 cells)
host: Darwin 25.5.0 aarch64 (mac)
date: 2026-09-10
build: a91c6882 (includes the patches-BFS prefilter of 800b295f)
reference: cjxl v0.12 from .ci-libjxl/tools/cjxl -- NOT the packaged v0.11.1,
           per the version rule in CLAUDE.md.
grid: 4 images (plots / web-screenshot / nature photo / NPS grayscale brochure)
      x sizes {64, 256, 1024, 2048} centre crops, metadata STRIPPED (the iCCP
      trap) and never upscaled -- plots and web-screenshot have no 2048 cell
      x efforts {3,5,7,9} x d {1.0, 4.0} x threads {1, 8}
timing: PROCESS wall, min of 5 (3 at 2048), arms alternated inside each repeat
        with the leading arm flipped every repeat. Both arms read the same PNG
        and write a real file, so process start, PNG decode and file write are
        in BOTH denominators. This is "how long does the user wait" -- it is NOT
        an encode-only ratio and must not be quoted as one.

